      "section": "Part I",
      "number": 3,
      "prompt": "A movie theatre charges Nakfa 4.00 for adults and Nakfa 1.50 for children under 15. One day when 325 people paid for admission, the total receipts were Nakfa 1025. How many of them were adults?",
      "options": [
        "175",
        "110",
        "125",
        "255",
        "None of the above."
      ],
      "correct_index": 4,
      "explanation_steps": [
        "Let a be the number of adults. Then children = 325 − a.",
        "4a + 1.5(325 − a) = 1025.",
        "4a + 487.5 − 1.5a = 1025, so 2.5a = 537.5 and a = 215.",
        "215 is not among A–D. Answer: E."
      ],
      "topics": [
        "alg-linear-equations"
      ],
      "unit_links": [],
      "similar_questions": []
